--- docs/sota_sprint/benchmark_spec.md ---
     1	# SOTA sprint: frozen benchmark specification (Agent E)
     2	
     3	Registered 2026-11-03 on branch `research/sota-sprint-24` (from `origin/main` 2171689) before any
     4	sprint run. Code: [scripts/sota_sprint/bench.py](../../scripts/sota_sprint/bench.py).
     5	
     6	* Contract: T=2000, hard B=200, c_q=.05, c_s=5, alpha=.05, release-before-act, delay >= 1, common
     7	  simulator `scripts/promising_directions/sota/simulator.py`. J = loss + .05 labels + 5 switches.
     8	* Paired streams: synthetic seed s of regime R = `SeedSequence([seed_base, sha(R), s])`; every policy
     9	  replays the same stream with a private generator.
    10	* Development screening: seed base 2026110501 (unused before), 20 seeds per environment, environments
    11	  from `DEV_ENVS` only (Atlas v2 F0-F9 + sprint additions S_* + budget variants `@B100`, `@B400`).
    12	* Validation (registered later, before any validation run): fresh seed base, 100 paired seeds, the
    13	  Atlas v2 V_* regimes plus new instances; null safety additionally on >= 500 null seeds.
    14	* Null-safety bound: promotion rate <= .0936 on every null regime incl. rho=.8 and rho=.95 Markov
    15	  nulls (Atlas v2 Amendment 2). 20-seed rates are screening diagnostics, not evidence of safety.
    16	* Comparators: `CERTIFIED_PUBLISHED` (strongest certified class, chosen per regime on the same seeds),
    17	  `UNCERTIFIED_PUBLISHED`, internal earlier candidates (QSG, QSG-env8, FLQ, RMM, LRMD, P7s; never
    18	  counted as published SOTA), controls. Author-faithful status per method is in
    19	  `docs/promising_directions/sota/SOTA_IMPLEMENTATION_VALIDATION.md`; every row here is a
    20	  common-contract port unless stated.
    21	* Primary statistic: paired Delta J = J(candidate) - J(comparator), 95% t-interval over seeds.
    22	* Runner/analysis: `scripts/sota_sprint/screen.py`, `scripts/sota_sprint/analyze.py`.

--- docs/sota_sprint/validation_protocol.md ---
     1	# SOTA sprint: locked validation protocol
     2	
     3	Locked 2026-11-03, after the 24-candidate development screen and before any validation run. The
     4	validation regimes and seeds were registered earlier in `scripts/sota_sprint/validation_spec.py`
     5	(commit 39d25ce, before any family reported). Nothing below may be changed after the first
     6	validation row is written; deviations are reported as deviations.
     7	
     8	## Seeds and data
     9	* Synthetic: seed base 2026110601, 100 paired seeds per regime, regimes `VAL_REGIMES` (13 Atlas v2
    10	  V_* instances, which had only been run with base 2026110399, plus 8 new W_* instances).
    11	* Null safety: seed base 2026110602, 1000 seeds on each regime in `NULL_REGIMES`
    12	  (V_null, V_worse, V_null_dep_r5, V_null_dep_r8, W_null_dep_r9, W_null_dep_r95, W_worse_dep_r8).
    13	* Real data (secondary, descriptive): the nine cached streams with episode-level inference and 20
    14	  policy seeds at base 2026110603. These streams were exposed in Atlas v2 development; no real-data
    15	  SOTA claim can be made from them.
    16	
    17	## Advanced candidates (at most two per family, chosen from development evidence)
    18	| family | candidates | host / control |
    19	|---|---|---|
    20	| A | A5b, A1b | QSG; A1b is A5b without adaptive density |
    21	| B | B2 | rmm:gated_deployment+RMM |
    22	| C | C2, C6 | gated_adaptive_range+front, gated_adaptive_range+pace_tuned |
    23	| D | D1, D2 | model_picker_adapter, cams_adapter |
    24	| combinations | chosen from the combination screen by the rule in H4 | as in the combination ledger |
    25	
    26	## Comparators
    27	* Certified published (`bench.CERTIFIED_PUBLISHED`): gated_deployment, gated_adaptive_range,
    28	  gated_adaptive_range+front, discern_style (corrected), discern_design_floor,
    29	  SMCS+retain-incumbent, xu_acquisition_only. Also the Choe-Ramdas-style EB comparators
    30	  choe_ramdas_eb and choe_ramdas_eb+front, which are added to the certified class for every
    31	  validation contrast.
    32	* Uncertified published: model_picker_adapter, model_selector_causal, online_llm_picker,
    33	  cams_adapter, variance_min_ipw, gong_zhang_paid_obs, qiu_delayed_movement, ryabchenko_capacity.
    34	* Internal (never "SOTA"): QSG, QSG-env8, gated_deployment+QCE+front, RMM, LRMD, P7s. Control:
    35	  never-switch, economic_replacement.
    36	* "Strongest applicable comparator" = the comparator in the stated class with the lowest mean cost
    37	  on that regime on the same seeds (selected after the fact, conservative for the candidate).
    38	
    39	## Hypotheses
    40	**H1, primary (reliability at matched cost; A5b).** All three parts must hold:
    41	1. (Safety) A5b's promotion rate is <= .0936 on every NULL_REGIMES regime over 1000 seeds.
    42	2. (Comparator failure) Every certified published comparator, including both Choe-Ramdas-style
    43	   ports, has a promotion rate above .0936 with Wilson 95% lower bound above .05 on at least one
    44	   NULL_REGIMES regime. Otherwise H1 is restated against the comparators that pass.
    45	3. (Non-inferior cost) On the iid stationary alternatives {V_better_a, V_better_b, V_better_c,
    46	   V_near, W_delay600_better}, the upper 95% bound of J(A5b) - J(strongest certified published)
    47	   is <= +5 on at least 4 of 5 regimes. The margin is 5 cost units per 2000 events, about 1.3% of
    48	   cost.
    49	   
    50	   Known dev losses are declared and reported but are not part of H1: V_bursty; dependent
    51	   alternatives V_dep_better_r5, W_better_dep_r7, W_better_dep_r9; change regimes V_late_600,
    52	   W_late_1000, V_reversal_1000, W_reversal_700, V_recurrent.
    53	
    54	   If H1 holds, the claim is: "the only method in the comparison whose false-promotion rate stays
    55	   within the registered bound under persistence up to rho = .95, at cost non-inferior to the
    56	   strongest certified published method on iid stationary alternatives."
    57	
    58	**H2 (cost superiority; secondary).** Holm-adjusted paired Delta J < 0 against the strongest
    59	certified published comparator, over the 5 iid stationary regimes above, for A5b, D1, D2, C2 and
    60	C6 (one Holm family per candidate). A cost superiority claim for a candidate is admissible only if
    61	that candidate also meets H1-part-1 safety; otherwise it is reported as "cheaper but unsafe".
    62	
    63	**H3 (mechanism attribution).** For each of A5b vs A1b (adaptive density), B2 vs its host on
    64	V_reversal_1000 and W_reversal_700 (rollback), and D1 vs model_picker_adapter on nulls, report the
    65	paired difference; this is descriptive.
    66	
    67	**H4 (combinations).** A combination advances to validation only if, on the 20-seed combination
    68	screen, its 95% CI vs its parent is below 0 on at least one targeted regime, with no null regime
    69	promotion above 2/20. Advanced combinations are tested under H1/H2 exactly as A5b.
    70	
    71	## Verdict rule
    72	`SOTA_MET` requires H1 (or H2 with safety) for at least one candidate on fresh synthetic seeds,
    73	plus a successful independent result-to-claim review of that exact claim. Real-data evidence on
    74	exposed streams is descriptive. The task's success gate requires independent real-data validation
    75	for a real-data claim, so any SOTA verdict is scoped "synthetic, under the declared Markov
    76	dependence class".
    77	
    78	## Amendment 1 (2026-11-03, before any validation row was read)
    79	A strict re-read of the brief (Phase 6: "at least the strongest two candidates per family should advance
    80	where functioning candidates exist") found Family B had only one advanced candidate. B5 (largest
    81	reversal gain vs host in development) is added as B's second candidate. It runs in a supplemental job on
    82	the same validation seed bases and regimes (streams are keyed by seed base, regime and seed, so rows pair
    83	with the main run by seed). It is evaluated under H3 (vs host on change regimes) and the H1-part-1 safety
    84	check. The two other changes are bookkeeping: the gate re-screen of all 24 at the committed revision
    85	(Phase 5 traceability) and the fresh real-data protocol (`fresh_real_protocol.md`, external validation).
    86	
    87	## Amendment 2 (2026-11-03, before any validation row was read)
    88	This amendment responds to the milestone 1-2 review (`review_milestone12.md`). The lead confirms that no
    89	validation record, log line or summary had been opened when it was committed. It supersedes H1 and H2
    90	where they conflict. Every original metric is still reported.
    91	
    92	* **O1 (stop rule carried over; claim wording).**
    93	  * **H0 restores the Atlas v2 registered stop rule verbatim** (Atlas v2 report section 9):
    94	    * Test a persistence-robust certified variant (A5b; A1b as its density-off control) against
    95	      xu_acquisition_only and tuned non-uniform pacing (gated_adaptive_range+pace_tuned).
    96	    * Success requires promotion <= .094 at rho=.8 and rho=.95, and paired CI < 0 against the stronger
    97	      of the two baselines on >= 4 of the 6 stationary alternatives {V_better_a, V_better_b, V_better_c,
    98	      V_dep_better_r5, V_near, V_bursty}. **If H0 fails, no cost-SOTA claim is made for A5b.**
    99	  * The H1 claim no longer says "only".
   100	  * H1 part 2 is replaced by a Pareto statement. Every certified published comparator must either
   101	    (a) fail a NULL_REGIMES null, meaning point rate > .0936 and Wilson 95% lower bound > .05, or
   102	    (b) be cost-dominated by A5b, meaning the 95% upper bound of J(A5b) - J(comparator) is < 0 on
   103	    >= 3 of the 6 stationary alternatives above.
   104	  * Every comparator is listed with its status.
   105	* **O2 (class dependence).**
   106	  * Any safety claim names the class: a stationary first-order homogeneous Markov sign in event time,
   107	    with p <= 1/2 and any rho, independent of disagreement arrivals, under constant delay.
   108	  * Two out-of-class nulls (`ooc_regimes.py`) run descriptively at 1000 seeds, base 2026110605, for
   109	    every candidate and certified comparator. They are reported next to the in-class nulls; they are
   110	    not part of H1.
   111	* **O3 (bursty).**
   112	  * Part 3 is also reported as k/6 including V_bursty.
   113	  * If A5b is not non-inferior on V_bursty, the claim is restricted to Bernoulli (non-bursty)
   114	    disagreement arrivals.
   115	  * The claim states that A5b has near-zero power against persistent alternatives.
   116	* **O4 (harm).** Every null reports harm: mean J minus never-switch J. Promotion rate alone is not
   117	  treated as harm.
   118	* **O5 (comparators).**
   119	  * choe_ramdas_eb is documented as the query-conditional PrPl-EB port (= DiscernQCE); it is not
   120	    author code.
   121	  * The betting-CS query-conditional ports gated_deployment+QCE and gated_deployment+QCE+front join the
   122	    certified comparator class as a supplemental run on the same seeds.
   123	  * The IPW betting form is discern_style/gated_adaptive_range (already in the class).
   124	  * Waudby-Smith et al. 2022 is NOT implemented, a recorded gap.
