     1	# Family A: dependence-aware certification. Screening results
     2	
     3	Status: development screening (20 dev seeds, base 2026110501) plus a 300-seed null check (base
     4	2026110511) for the promising candidates. Nothing here is validation evidence. Code:
     5	`scripts/sota_sprint/fam_a.py`; tests: `tests/sota_sprint/test_fam_a.py` (16 pass). Ledger:
     6	`ledger.json`. Analyzer tables: `screen1.md` (A1-A6), `screen2.md` (round-2 dev variants
     7	A1b/A5b/A6b/A2b), `ablations.md`, `null300.md`. Raw records: `outputs/sota_sprint/A/` (gitignored).
     8	
     9	## Candidates
    10	
    11	| id | mechanism | null class / validity |
    12	|---|---|---|
    13	| A1 | sequential universal inference: Markov-mixture numerator / rigorous upper bound on the null sup of the gap-indexed Markov likelihood; sparse started mixture | stationary 2-state Markov sign, p <= 1/2, **any rho in [0,1]**; P(false promotion) <= alpha (Ville) |
    14	| A2 | adaptive query density: min event gap g* = min{g: rho_hat^g <= .25}, rho_hat = gap-indexed MLE from released labels; QSG iid evidence | not certified under dependence |
    15	| A3 | dual-clock: new tests start at the next outcome in query order (in-flight outcomes used); front-loading pauses when in-flight queries exceed 2x projected need | QSG's (iid) |
    16	| A4 | bet only on outcomes following an unfavourable one: P(z=1 given prev=0) = (1-rho^g)p <= 1/2 for any rho | same class as A1 |
    17	| A5 | A1 + A2 | as A1 |
    18	| A6 | A1 + A2 + A3 | as A1 |
