     1	# SOTA sprint family B: nonstationary detection and recovery (screening, dev seeds)
     2	
     3	Status: development screening only (20 dev seeds, seed base 2026110501; null check 300 seeds at
     4	2026110512). These are descriptive screening results, not confirmatory evidence. Code:
     5	`scripts/sota_sprint/fam_b.py` (`RecoveryMonitor`, subclass of the Atlas v2 RMM host). Tests:
     6	`tests/sota_sprint/test_fam_b.py` (22 pass). Ledger: `ledger.json`; per-family numbers:
     7	`key_numbers.json`; analyze.py output: `screen1.json/.md`.
     8	
     9	## Host and what is controlled
    10	
    11	Host = `rmm:gated_deployment+RMM`. `B0_host` (all mechanisms off) reproduces it exactly: identical
    12	net cost and deployment path on all 240 dev jobs.
    13	
    14	* **First promotion** (all B variants): base Gated CS at alpha/2 plus the label-clock restart-mixture
    15	  SR e-detector at alpha/2. Under the iid conditional null (challenger correct on a queried
    16	  disagreement with probability <= 1/2, independent of the past) P(any promotion) <= alpha = .05.
    17	  Reserve and deadline only change predictable query rules, and the detector uses unweighted
    18	  label-clock outcomes, so this bound is unchanged. Empirical: F0_null 1-3/300 promotions.
    19	* **After the first promotion**: the B2 rollback is a detector alarm at alpha_rb = .10 against
    20	  "the deployed challenger is not worse". A false rollback is a cost (2 c_s plus time on the
    21	  incumbent), not a safety error; observed false rollbacks: 0 on F0_better/F9_bursty_better, at
    22	  most .05-.10 per run on F4_recurrent. Re-promotions after a rollback spend (alpha_base +
    23	  alpha_det)/2^k. **Not controlled**: detection delay/time on a model that has become worse;
    24	  anything under serial dependence; the host's own rollback detector in B1/B3/B4 (alpha=.05).
    25	* **Dependence (rho=.8) null fails for everyone in this line**: F5_dep_null_r8 promotion on 300
    26	  seeds: host .150, B2 .150, B5 .123, B6 .150, B2+B4 .170 (bound .0936). No B mechanism addresses it.
    27	
    28	## Results (20 dev seeds; family = per-seed mean of paired differences; 95% t-interval)
    29	
    30	Families: late = F1_late_800, F1_late_1200, S_late_1500; reversal = F3_reversal_800,
    31	S_reversal_400; recurrent = F4_recurrent; transient = F2_transient, S_transient_short;
    32	stationary_alt = F0_better, F9_bursty_better. Negative favours the candidate.
    33	
    34	| cand | late vs host | reversal vs host | recurrent vs host | stat_alt vs host | reversal vs best cert | recurrent vs best cert | late vs best cert |
    35	|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
    36	| host | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | +28.5 [+16.6,+40.4] | +21.7 [+13.3,+30.1] | -10.6 [-14.2,-7.0] |
