     1	"""SOTA sprint family B: nonstationary detection and recovery on top of Gated+RMM.
     2	
     3	Host: ``rmm:gated_deployment+RMM`` (RestartMixtureMonitor around GatedDeploymentStop, base at
     4	alpha/2, label-clock restart-mixture SR e-detector at alpha/2, continued paced acquisition).
     5	``RecoveryMonitor`` subclasses the host and adds four switchable mechanisms:
     6	
     7	* reserve (B1): before the first deployment decision (a promotion, by detector or base, or the
     8	  base's own "discard" verdict) the base and the monitor pacer see ``remaining - ceil(rho B)``;
     9	  the held ``rho B`` labels are released only after that decision, for monitoring.
    10	* rollback (B2): after a promotion the rollback detector is a restart-mixture SR e-detector at
    11	  ``alpha_rb = .10`` whose start grid covers the budget actually left at promotion (less prior
    12	  dilution than the host's grid over all of B), with a horizon gate: no rollback when fewer than
    13	  ``h_min = ceil(c_s / g_ref)`` events remain (it cannot repay its switch cost). After a rollback
    14	  the base is restarted at ``alpha_base / 2^k`` and the promotion detector at ``alpha_det / 2^j``.
    15	* multiscale (B3): the detector is a weighted mixture of three restart grids (one start at the
    16	  first label; starts every 25 labels; starts every 5 labels) over a wider bet grid.
    17	* deadline (B4): no label is bought (by base or monitor) whose release ``t + delay`` falls after
    18	  ``T - h_min``; the monitor pacer spreads the remaining budget over the window that is still
    19	  useful, and skips a label when even all outstanding plus all still-purchasable labels at the
    20	  maximal bet could not push the detector over its threshold before the deadline.
    21	
    22	Error accounting (iid conditional null: on queried disagreements the challenger is correct with
    23	probability <= 1/2, independently of the past and of the predictable query rule).
    24	* First promotion: base CS at alpha/2 plus detector at alpha/2 (Ville on the mixture), so
    25	  P(any promotion) <= alpha. Reserve and deadline only change predictable propensities or stop
    26	  querying, and the detector uses unweighted label-clock outcomes, so this is unchanged.
    27	* After a promotion: a rollback is an alarm of a detector at level alpha_rb against the null
    28	  "the deployed challenger is not worse"; a false rollback is a COST (two switches plus time on the
    29	  incumbent), not a safety error, and we report its empirical rate. Re-promotions after a
    30	  rollback spend (alpha_det + alpha_base)/2^k, so under a global null after the rollback the
    31	  k-th re-promotion has probability <= alpha/2^k. NOT controlled: time on a model that became
    32	  worse (detection delay), anything under serial dependence (rho > 0), the host's own rollback
    33	  at alpha (B0/B1/B3/B4 keep the host's rollback detector at alpha=.05 over a grid on B).
    34	"""
    35	
    36	from __future__ import annotations
    37	
