     1	"""Family C (SOTA sprint): label acquisition and economics on certified hosts (Agent C).
     2	
     3	Every candidate here changes ONLY the acquisition rule of an existing certified host; the host's
     4	confidence sequence (CS), stopping rule and deployment rule are untouched.
     5	
     6	Hosts
     7	-----
     8	* ``gated_adaptive_range`` (MOPE off-policy CS, per-step ``wmax_t = 1/q_t``), and its ``+front``.
     9	* ``discern_design_floor`` (corrected DISCERN PrPl-EB CS, ``pi_min = .25``, ``c = 4``) and
    10	  ``discern_style`` (``pi_min = .05``).
    11	* ``QSG`` (query-conditional started mixture; no importance weights).
    12	
    13	Acquisition actions
    14	-------------------
    15	At each event a controller returns ``(pi, q)``: the event is *recorded* in the host CS with
    16	probability ``pi`` (a predictable coin from the host's private generator, drawn before the label
    17	exists) and, if recorded and a disagreement, its label is requested with propensity ``q``. The
    18	issue-time ``q`` travels with the request (``QueryRequest.probability``) and the host uses
    19	``1/q`` from ``ReleasedFeedback.query_probability`` as the importance weight; for the gated host the
    20	per-step range ``wmax_t = max(1/q, 2)`` is also fixed at issue. An unrecorded event never enters
    21	the CS (no increment, no block on the ordered queue).
    22	
    23	The cheapest valid "skip" differs by host and is declared (``skip_action``):
    24	* gated (adaptive range): skip = unrecorded (``pi = 0``). A recorded low-``q`` event would set
    25	  ``wmax_t = 1/q`` and an exact zero for most such events, which costs wealth.
    26	* DISCERN (fixed range ``c = 1/pi_min``): skip = record with ``q = pi_min`` (the CS is
    27	  event-clock-limited under ``lam_max``, so dropping events slows it; ``q = pi_min`` keeps
    28	  ``|Z| <= c``).
    29	
    30	Validity (stated per candidate in docs/sota_sprint/family_c/README.md)
    31	----------------------------------------------------------------------
    32	For the propensity-weighted hosts the false-promotion guarantee needs (i) ``q_t`` predictable
    33	(it reads only the past released labels, the pending count, predictions of event t and the
    34	budget), (ii) ``q_t >= 1/wmax_t`` where the CS needs it (gated: ``wmax_t = 1/q_t`` exactly;
    35	DISCERN: ``q_t >= pi_min``, enforced by clamping), and (iii) the recorded subsequence chosen by a
    36	predictable coin. (iii) is optional skipping of a test supermartingale: under the pointwise
    37	promotion null ``E[l0 - l1 | F_{t-1}, predictions_t] <= 0`` every recorded increment has
    38	conditional mean on the null side, so Ville's inequality still applies. Under a non-stationary
    39	alternative the CS then targets the average over *recorded* events, not over all events (the
    40	same estimand change QCE records). No candidate reads the label of the event it decides on.
    41	
    42	Factories have the sprint signature ``f(T, B, cs, cq, alpha, delay, r) -> Policy``.
    43	"""
    44	
    45	from __future__ import annotations
    46	
    47	import sys
    48	from pathlib import Path
    49	
    50	import numpy as np
    51	
    52	ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
    53	for _p in (ROOT / "scripts/failure_atlas_v2_flq", ROOT / "scripts/promising_directions/sota",
    54	           ROOT / "scripts/promising_directions/sota/competitors"):
