     1	"""Comparators added after the Agent F prior-art audit (2026-11-03).
     2	
     3	Choe & Ramdas, "Comparing sequential forecasters" (Oper. Res. 2024, arXiv:2110.00115) and Henzi &
     4	Ziegel (Biometrika 2022, arXiv:2103.08402) give anytime-valid comparisons of two forecasters under
     5	ARBITRARY dependence, for the null that the running average of conditional mean loss differences is
     6	<= 0. Their constructions are empirical-Bernstein / betting confidence sequences on paired loss
     7	differences with full observation. Under a hard label budget no author rule exists for which events
     8	to label; the common-contract port below runs the Waudby-Smith-Ramdas predictable-plug-in EB CS
     9	(the same EB family Choe-Ramdas use) on query-conditional paired differences Y in [-1, 1], with
    10	uniform paced acquisition ("choe_ramdas_eb") or every disagreement queried while undecided
    11	("+front"). This is an adapter, not author code; it reuses DiscernQCE's fidelity-checked PrPl-EB CS.
    12	
    13	Note on nulls: these methods control the time-averaged CONDITIONAL mean. Under a persistent Markov
    14	null with marginal p = 1/2 that average is positive during runs, so a promotion there is correct
    15	for their null and a false promotion for the marginal null the ShiftLab bound targets.
    16	"""
    17	
    18	from __future__ import annotations
    19	
    20	import sys
    21	from pathlib import Path
    22	
    23	_FLQ = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] / "failure_atlas_v2_flq"
    24	if str(_FLQ) not in sys.path:
    25	    sys.path.insert(0, str(_FLQ))
